NAME
       installer - install PureC OS from the live medium to a disk

SYNOPSIS
       /sbin/installer [--config FILE]

DESCRIPTION
       A menu installer in the style of archinstall. Run it as root on a text
       console. The main menu lists every setting with its current value;
       open any item in any order, change it, come back, then choose Install.

           Disk configuration    sda 20.0 GiB  wipe, default layout
           Hostname              purec
           Root password         not set
           User accounts         none (only root)
           Profile               Minimal
           Additional packages   none
           Timezone              UTC
           ----------------------------------------
           Save configuration
           Install
           Abort

       Values in red are missing; Install refuses to start until the disk and
       the root password are set.

KEYS
       Up/Down (or j/k), Home/End, PgUp/PgDn  move
       Enter                                  open / select
       Space                                  toggle (Additional packages)
       /                                      search in a list (Timezone ...)
       Esc or q                               back / abort

MENU
       Disk configuration
              choose the disk; it is erased and laid out automatically: GPT,
              EFI partition with Limine, ext2 root, swap on ATA/SATA disks
       Root password, Hostname, Timezone
       User accounts
              Add a user (name, full name, password, superuser = group wheel
              and sudo); select a user to change the password, promote or
              demote, delete; Confirm and exit
       Profile
              Minimal (text consoles) or Desktop: the package "userspace" is
              downloaded from GitHub after the base system and graphical.target
              becomes the default (asks for the repository address when it is
              not in [trusted] of /etc/pkg/pkg.conf)
       Additional packages
              tick packages from the trusted repositories in /etc/pkg/pkg.conf
       Save configuration
              write the choices without passwords (default
              /root/purec-install.conf); --config FILE loads them, passwords
              are then asked in the menu
       Install
              shows a final Yes/No (No is preselected), then the kernel writes
              the disk with a progress bar, mkinitcpio -u writes root=UUID=,
              pkg installs the packages, /etc/init/default.target is set and
              the installer offers to reboot

FILES
       /etc/pkg/pkg.conf, /etc/init/default.target, /root/purec-install.conf

SEE ALSO
       pkg(8), init(8), mkinitcpio(8), sudo(8)
